#: ../../source/api/lab/isaaclab.sim.views.rst:13
msgid "XForm Prim View"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:1 of
msgid "Bases: :py:class:`object`"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:3 of
msgid ""
"This class provides efficient batch operations for getting and setting "
"poses (position and orientation) of multiple prims at once using torch "
"tensors. It is designed for scenarios where you need to manipulate many "
"prims simultaneously, such as in multi-agent simulations or large-scale "
"procedural generation."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:7 of
msgid "The class supports both world-space and local-space pose operations:"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:9 of
msgid "**World poses**: Positions and orientations in the global world frame"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:10 of
msgid "**Local poses**: Positions and orientations relative to each prim's parent"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:13 of
msgid "**Fabric and Physics Simulation:**"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:15 of
msgid ""
"This view operates directly on USD attributes. When **Fabric** (NVIDIA's "
"USD runtime optimization) is enabled, physics simulation updates are "
"written to Fabric's internal representation and **not propagated back to "
"USD attributes**. This causes the following issues:"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:19 of
msgid ""
"Reading poses via :func:`get_world_poses()` or :func:`get_local_poses()` "
"will return **stale USD data** which does not reflect the actual physics "
"state"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:21 of
msgid ""
"Writing poses via :func:`set_world_poses()` or :func:`set_local_poses()` "
"will update USD, but **physics simulation will not see these changes**."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:24 of
msgid ""
"**Solution:** For prims with physics components (rigid bodies, "
"articulations), use :mod:`isaaclab.assets` classes (e.g., "
":class:`~isaaclab.assets.RigidObject`, "
":class:`~isaaclab.assets.Articulation`) which use PhysX tensor APIs that "
"work correctly with Fabric."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:29 of
msgid "**When to use XformPrimView:**"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:31 of
msgid "Non-physics prims (markers, visual elements, cameras without physics)"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:32 of
msgid "Setting initial poses before simulation starts"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:33 of
msgid "Non-Fabric workflows"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:35 of
msgid ""
"For more information on Fabric, please refer to the `Fabric "
"documentation`_."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:40 of
msgid "**Performance Considerations:**"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:42 of
msgid "Tensor operations are performed on the specified device (CPU/CUDA)"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:43 of
msgid "USD write operations use ``Sdf.ChangeBlock`` for batched updates"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:44 of
msgid ""
"Getting poses involves USD API calls and cannot be fully accelerated on "
"GPU"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:45 of
msgid "For maximum performance, minimize get/set operations within tight loops"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:48 of
msgid "**Transform Requirements:**"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:50 of
msgid ""
"All prims in the view must be Xformable and have standardized transform "
"operations: ``[translate, orient, scale]``. Non-standard prims will raise"
" a ValueError during initialization if :attr:`validate_xform_ops` is "
"True. Please use the function "
":func:`isaaclab.sim.utils.standardize_xform_ops` to prepare prims before "
"using this view."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.views.xform_prim_view.XformPrimView:56 of
msgid ""
"This class operates at the USD default time code. Any animation or time-"
"sampled data will not be affected by write operations. For animated "
"transforms, you need to handle time-sampled keyframes separately."
msgstr ""

